The code statements that lead to the bug are:
memcpy(ad + len, adv->adv_data, adv->adv_data_len);
Reason:
The `memcpy` copies `adv->adv_data_len` bytes into the temporary buffer `ad` starting at offset `len` without first verifying that `adv->adv_data_len` does not exceed the remaining space (`sizeof(ad) - len`). When an existing advertising instance already holds the maximum extended advertising payload, the combined size can exceed the buffer capacity, causing a buffer overflow.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (adv->adv_data_len > sizeof(ad) - len) {
    bt_dev_err(hdev, "No room for Broadcast Announcement");
    return -EINVAL;
}
Reason:
The added check ensures that the combined size of the existing advertising data (`adv->adv_data_len`) and the newly appended Broadcast Announcement service data (`len`) does not exceed the size of the temporary buffer (`sizeof(ad)`). If it does, the operation is rejected with an error, preventing the buffer overflow and keeping the existing advertising data intact.

